  "source": "JoyPro curated on the maker's photo (2026-10-11), the FarmStick seen from the front-left and above, hand-rest control face toward the camera, front of the base at the bottom",
  "mappingSource": "SimTask FarmStick user manual p.17-18 \"Mapping of buttons and axes\" (https://ts.thrustmaster.com/download/accessories/Manuals/Farmstick/SimTask_FarmStick_User_Manual.pdf): base 1-6 left module, 7-12 right module, 13 / 18 angled front buttons, 14 / 15 / 16 front row, 17 START; hand rest 19-21 upper button row, 24 / 23 / 22 lower row (left to right), 25 thumbwheel push (32 / 33 wheel in Drive mode), 26 mini-stick push, 27 / 28 left rocker, 29 / 30 right rocker (Drive mode); matches the catalog",
  "confidence": "medium",
  "note": "The right base module carries tiny printed numbers 7-12 on its centre strip (7 / 9 / 11 on the right column, 8 / 10 / 12 on the left column, from the stick outward); placed by those labels (map=medium, the labels are small). The left base module (1-6) is seen at a grazing angle: its six buttons are visible as two strips of three, but which strip is the 1 / 3 / 5 row is derived from the manual figure and the mirrored right module only, so 1-6 are candidates (map=low). Direction words: the catalog's rocker up / down and wheel up / down are matched to the upper / lower number of the manual figure (front / rear end of the control), so map=medium for those six parts. Modes: buttons 27-33 (rockers and thumbwheel up / down) exist only in Drive mode; in Work mode the rockers and the wheel are axes 6-8 (manual p.18). Mapping is identical in right- and left-handed mode (manual p.17).",
